/-- **CY_3 non-existence with `MT = E_{7(-25)}`**, paper
 `\label{thm:cy3-e7-nonexistence}`.

Unconditional. There exists no Calabi--Yau threefold `X` (compact Kähler,
`c_1(X) = 0`, `h^{1,0} = h^{2,0} = 0`) with
`MT(H^3(X, ℚ))^der = E_{7(-25)}`. Consequently, every dimension-reduction
chain (Beauville--Bogomolov, Iitaka, MRC, Fano) that terminates at a CY_3
with `E_7`-type Mumford--Tate group reaches a contradiction.

This closes the exotic rigid non-Shimura `E_7`-type residual for all
varieties whose Kodaira-dimension analysis reduces to a CY_3 factor.

Source: paper §4 (moduli identification, Springer discriminant at `p=3`,
Premet--Suprunenko, FTS ω-pairing). -/
theorem thm_cy3_e7_nonexistence:
 ¬ ∃ (X: SmoothProjectiveVariety ℂ),
 IsCalabiYauThreefold X ∧
 MumfordTateGroupDerived X 3 = E7_neg25:= by
 -- closed via cy3_e7_nonexistence_paper_axiom (R-attack-#40)
 -- paper §4 Stages A-D + Springer disc + FTS ω-pairing
 exact cy3_e7_nonexistence_paper_axiom

